-# P2a — design, spec, measurements (no code) — 2026-09-26
-
-Plan: `PLAN-app-master-2026-09.md:147-150` (P2 "Speed"), `:340-342` (§8 "Before P2"),
-`:70-74` (area verdict). ROUTE-OK job (Codex slot held by P1a).
-
-## 1. Measured load today
-
-`app/index.html:1-145` script/link order, bytes by `wc -c` (2026-09-26). Shared/chrome (loads on
-every page): `index.html` 14,439 · `data/fonts.js` (`:36`) 129,691 · 6 CSS files 165,497
-(`tokens.css` 8,959, `base.css` 1,015, `layout.css` 15,064, `components.css` 69,000,
-`print.css` 17,161, `views.css` 54,298) · `ambient-library.mp4`+`.jpg`+`icon-96.png`+`icon-180.png`
-437,045 (matches `G-perf.md` media figure) · `data/modules.js` (`:114`, MODULES+LOCKED_MODULES,
-every subject's chapter list) 27,280 · 11 shared `js/*.js` (`storage.js`…`boot.js`, `:133-143`)
-277,461 · two empty-run aggregators `data/questions.js`+`data/theory.js` (`:127,132`) 4,299.
-
-Per-subject data (`:115-131`, in load order): **ent** `questions.ent.js` 7,785,695 +
-`cases.ent.js` 220,744 + `theory.ent.js` 683,667 = 8,690,106 · **pediatrics**
-`questions.peds.js`+`.ep.js`+`.ep2.js` 1,540,772+2,075,143+1,699,737 + `cases.peds.js` 625 +
-`theory.peds.js` 925,240 = 6,241,517 · **ophtho** `questions.ophtho.js`+`.ep.js`+`.ep2.js`
-4,706,093+786,187+372,885 + `cases.ophtho.js` 630 + `theory.ophtho.js` 792,670 = 6,658,465 ·
-**neuropsych** `questions.neuro.js` 2,524,330 + `cases.neuro.js` 33,287 + `theory.neuro.js`
-896,498 = 3,454,115.
-
-**Grand total, all 30 `<script src>` data/JS tags + CSS + media**: sums to 26,080,321 B, matching
-`G-perf.md:80-81` Round 3 (authoritative; this table reproduces it, gap <0.03%, not
-re-investigated).
-
-**Home needs**: shared chrome above = **1,055,663 B** (index.html + fonts + CSS + media +
-modules.js + 11 app scripts + empty aggregators). This is **already over the plan's <1 MB
-target by ~55 KB** even with zero subject payload — `fonts.js` (129,691 B, inline in `<head>`
-before CSS, `CLAUDE.md:31`) and `components.css`+`views.css` (123,298 B) are the largest
-shared items; P2 will need to trim shared bytes too, not only defer subject data, to clear 1 MB.
-
-**One subject needs**, on top of that floor: ENT (largest) adds 8,690,106 B; neuropsych
-(smallest) adds 3,454,115 B. All four dwarf the 1 MB target — confirms per-subject injection
-must defer every subject's data past first paint, none merged into it.
-
-## 2. Manifest design
-
-`app/data/manifest.js`, classic script, `var MANIFEST` — never `const` (a `const` fails to leave
-a `vm` eval, `MEMORY.md` "Validation state" fault 5-6; every other data file here uses `var` for
-the same reason, `CLAUDE.md:29-31`). Shape:
-
-```js
-var MANIFEST = {
-  ent:        { q:['data/questions.ent.js'], c:['data/cases.ent.js'], t:['data/theory.ent.js'],
-                bytes:{'data/questions.ent.js':7785695,'data/cases.ent.js':220744,
-                       'data/theory.ent.js':683667},
-                counts:{Q_ENT:<n>, C_ENT:<n>, T_ENT:<n-keys>} },
-  pediatrics: { q:['data/questions.peds.js','data/questions.peds.ep.js','data/questions.peds.ep2.js'],
-                c:['data/cases.peds.js'], t:['data/theory.peds.js'], bytes:{...}, counts:{...} },
-  ophtho:     { q:['data/questions.ophtho.js','data/questions.ophtho.ep.js','data/questions.ophtho.ep2.js'],
-                c:['data/cases.ophtho.js'], t:['data/theory.ophtho.js'], bytes:{...}, counts:{...} },
-  neuropsych: { q:['data/questions.neuro.js'], c:['data/cases.neuro.js'],
-                t:['data/theory.neuro.js'], bytes:{...}, counts:{...} }
-};
-```
-
-Keys match `storage.js:106-109`'s four `subjects` rows (`ent`/`pediatrics`/`ophtho`/
-`neuropsych`) — a loader indexes `MANIFEST[subjectId]` with no translation table. `counts`
-replaces `tools/validate/counts.json`, which P1a is hand-writing now as a stand-in
-("P2's manifest will replace it later", `p1a-gate-brief.md:37`). P2a does not touch
-`tools/validate/` (P1a's live write grant); P2 code should read `MANIFEST.<subject>.counts`
-where the validator reads `counts.json` today, keeping `counts.json` as a cross-check rather
-than deleting it.
-
-## 3. Injection design
-
-`QUESTIONS` consumers (grep, `app/js/*.js`): `boot.js:339`; `clepsydra.js:365,369,370,411,544,
-578`; `quiz.js:39,91,133,138,189,337,475,499,600,676,776,984,1002,1027,1035-1036,1167,1200,1213,
-1240`; `render.js:13,133,175-177,200`; `sessions.js:459`; `storage.js:277,278,280,285`
-(`qsIn`/`qsInModule`/`allQsInModule`/`banksPresent`); `theory.js:659`; `utils.js:72` (`deckAll`).
-`THEORY` is consumed the same shape (keyed access on the rebuilt object). All of the above read
-`QUESTIONS`/`THEORY`, never a raw per-subject global.
-
-The 16 per-subject `Q_*`/`C_*`/`T_*` globals have exactly **one** outside-data-file consumer:
-`storage.js:106-109`'s `subjects` table inside `warnSaveFailure.checkData` — an existence probe
-(`window[name]!==undefined`), not a value read. This is the seam: per-subject injection only
-needs the two rebuild functions re-runnable, not every call site above touched.
-`banksOf(q)` (never `bankOf(q)`, `CLAUDE.md:38-40`): defined `storage.js:261`; today's one
-`bankOf(` grep hit is that definition line plus its own warning comment (`storage.js:255,261`) —
-**0 stray call sites**, measured 2026-09-26; P2 must hold this at 0.
-
-**Order kept**: subjects → aggregators (`CLAUDE.md:31`). Injection appends `<script>` tags for
-`MANIFEST[subjectId].q/.c/.t` when a subject opens; each still sets its `window.Q_ENT=...` `var`
-unchanged (no data-file edit for P2a). Once a subject's scripts resolve (`onload` on the last,
-or `Promise.all`), call `rebuildQuestions(termId)`/`rebuildTheory(termId)` again — both already
-idempotent, filtering `Q_ALL`/`T_ALL` fresh each call (`questions.js:55-62`, `theory.js:26-34`),
-so a late subject just widens `Q_ALL`/`T_ALL` on the next call; no aggregator rewrite, only a
-rebuild trigger wired to "subject scripts landed".
-
-**Failure path** (`CLAUDE.md:33-35` timeout pattern): a subject script that 404s/throws must not
-strand the view. Each injected `<script>` gets `onerror` resolving its slot "missing" rather than
-rejecting the whole load; a subject timeout (shape of `loadSDK()`'s 8 s) rebuilds with whatever
-arrived; the existing `warnSaveFailure`/`checkData` banner (`storage.js:95-115`, already built to
-tolerate absent subjects) reports the gap instead of hanging — reused, not reinvented.
-
-## 4. "Before P2" migration protocol (§8, `PLAN:340-342`)
-
-Extends the existing validated export at `boot.js:191-289` (`exportData`/`checkedProgressState`/
-`importData` — brief's cited `191-284` runs a few lines short in this checkout; `199-265` is the
-schema check, `266-289`+ the merge-import). `mergeStates` (`gate.js:213-224`) and the Firestore
-transaction (`gate.js:280-294`) are the cloud counterpart.
-
-- **Versioned schema**: `exportData` writes `{v:2,saved,state:S}` (`boot.js:192`); `importData`
-  rejects `d.v!==2` (`boot.js:275`). Manifest loading changes *when* data arrives, not `S`'s
-  shape — no `v` bump. A "has seen per-subject loading" marker, if ever needed, goes under
-  `extra` in `checkedProgressState` (`boot.js:260-263`), never into `v`.
-- **Per-profile paths / field ownership**: no field in `S` is subject-scoped (all keyed by
-  question id); `checkedProgressState` never cross-checks an id against a loaded bank — no new
-  ownership table needed.
-- **Resumable markers**: `resumeByChapter` (`boot.js:236-237`) is chapter-keyed, not
-  loaded-subject-keyed. P2 must defer the "does `qid` still exist" check (`render.js:13` pattern)
-  until after that subject's rebuild, not at profile-load time.
-- **Old-client compatibility**: a pre-P2 client loads all data eagerly and reads the same `S`
-  untouched — an export from a P2 client should open on a pre-P2 client unchanged. Reasoning
-  only, UNVERIFIED by a runtime test (no-code brief).
-- **Unknown ids**: confirmed `checkedProgressState`/`mergeStates` check shape only, never id
-  membership (`boot.js:220-238`) — an id from an unloaded subject already survives merge
-  untouched; no new handling needed.
-- **Rollback**: `wardround.bak.<profileId>` (`bakRestore`, `boot.js:180-189`) is per-profile and
-  untouched by manifest work; the code-change rollback is the per-phase `git tag` (`PLAN:309`).
-- **Recovery fixtures — gap**: nothing seeds a *missing* or *late* subject script today. P1a's
-  fixture harness (`p1a-gate-brief.md:39-42`) covers data-file defects only. P2 needs one new
-  fixture: a manifest entry pointing at a 404'd file, asserting the view still renders via §3's
-  failure path.
-- **Export/import already ships** (`boot.js:191-289`); what's missing per §8 is only the two
-  items above (deferred unknown-id check, one recovery fixture) — not the export mechanism.
-
-## 5. Risks
-
-| Risk | file:line | P2 must pass |
-|---|---|---|
-| Home still over 1 MB even with subject data deferred | shared chrome measured 1,055,663 B, §1 | Home first load < 1 MB — shared bytes need trimming too, not only deferral |
-| Aggregator rebuild silently stale after late subject arrival | `data/questions.js:55-62`, `data/theory.js:26-34` (re-runnable; nothing calls them today except on term switch) | Every subject boots to its pre-change count: ent 2,240+82c · pediatrics 393+704+630 · ophtho 1,273+433+147 · neuropsych 1,047+7c (`MEMORY.md` "Validation state", 2026-09-25 recount, 6,956 total, 0 holes — re-measure at P2 exit) |
-| A rewritten bank check bypasses `banksOf` | `storage.js:255,261` | `bankOf(` outside the definition = **0**, measured today |
-| Failed subject script strands the view | no per-subject timeout exists (`CLAUDE.md:33-35` only covers Firebase) | new load path degrades via `warnSaveFailure`, never hangs |
-| `storage.js:106-109` table drifts from `MANIFEST` keys | both list the same 4 subject ids | grep both after any manifest edit |
-| `wardround.*` key rename | none proposed here | diff-only grep `wardround\.` before any P2 commit |
-
-## 6. Open questions for the owner
-
-1. `MANIFEST.<subject>.counts` — hand-authored (like P1a's `counts.json` now) or generated by a
-   script, and if generated, does that script live under `tools/` (P1a's current grant) or wait
-   for a P2 grant? Scope call, not a code fact.
-2. The missing/late-subject recovery fixture (§4) — P1a's harness or a new P2 fixture?
-3. The optional `extra` version marker (§4) — does any planned future code need to distinguish
-   an old-format profile from a new one? Nothing in the current code needs it yet.

