+## 5. Tooling, migration, checks
+
+- Validator replaces HTML script-tag discovery (`validate.js:7–10`) with `MANIFEST`, evaluates each
+  listed q/c/t classic file in its isolated VM, compares declared bytes/counts, and checks four ids.
+- Boot check evaluates manifest, injects each subject via loader, awaits each settlement, then reads
+  `QUESTIONS` and executes chapter rows (`boot-check.js:133,146–150`). Success equals declared
+  count; a bad path must show failure UI without hung route.
+- Exit: each subject independently reaches pre-P2 q/c/theory counts; `bankOf(` calls = 0 excluding
+  definition; deferred subjects never warn at boot; file cold-home <1,000,000 B.
+- Before ship export/import `wardround.*`, including an unloaded-subject answer/resume id.
+  `checkedProgressState` and `mergeStates` (`gate.js:202`) retain it. No schema bump: v2, global
+  qid ownership, old eager clients, and `wardround.bak.<profile>` remain. Add missing-script fixture
+  to P2 harness. No `extra` marker is needed.
 
